acy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "parents": [{"sha": "2b5f0416559d01b8d539220116bbf0098c736bf1", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/commits/2b5f0416559d01b8d539220116bbf0098c736bf1", "html_url": "https://github.com/ray-project/ray/commit/2b5f0416559d01b8d539220116bbf0098c736bf1"}]}, {"sha": "b5687a1aaa3dc72dfde9758e730607a4ab22afe4", "node_id": "C_kwDOBEmZvdoAKGI1Njg3YTFhYWEzZGM3MmRmZGU5NzU4ZTczMDYwN2E0YWIyMmFmZTQ", "commit": {"author": {"name": "Clark Zinzow", "email": "clarkzinzow@gmail.com", "date": "2022-10-06T16:42:16Z"}, "committer": {"name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com", "date": "2022-10-06T16:42:16Z"}, "message": "[Datasets] Bundle blocks smaller than batch size in `map_batches` tasks. (#28648)\n\nWhen blocks are smaller than the batch size in map_batches(), the actual size of batches provided to the UDF can be much smaller (order of magnitude) than the specified batch size, resulting in very poor batch mapping throughput when the UDF's performance is sensitive to the batch size (such as in batch inference on GPUs).\r\n\r\nThis PR optimistically sends multiple blocks to a single mapper task up to (but not past) the provided batch size, mitigating the case in which block size << batch size without needing a shuffle step.", "tree": {"sha": "6341e9d2ceede948b9685cc1f8a69ebc28da200c", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/git/trees/6341e9d2ceede948b9685cc1f8a69ebc28da200c"}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/git/commits/b5687a1aaa3dc72dfde9758e730607a4ab22afe4", "comment_count": 0, "verification": {"verified": true, "reason": "valid", "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJjPwVoCRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAAiiQIADMshPrmWLJwvpo0FEijWzE3\nMpP53vvWlc8+dWJP5Yo546l0sk8mS8e22BqW8sjDFPSRWEUNiFK4HJkXVwbvQVz8\nCzkePxxJRUbW+JJqqPZ1POgHVK+I1qnWTAuOkSmLHKHL1L6+KhuN58MWgOHPQlfC\nGb6zEd46eQIbhWohg9UTtA8mG/92X5jjjCFlR/n6iSdnvhtfUVkcaNaTWvIyiL6h\nYZnMd3zjnaMjrr6GdUGmhzYeeM1c+F2AQTqwHvCH8Jxo58VG1KNy+fl98C7CBRkp\n7DyidMMZkUxyTiMRcknsAEiUeNI/kq3shX/gYdEG1BARkHYg7/h/yA+xI9tWCA8=\n=mWS0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n", "payload": "tree 6341e9d2ceede948b9685cc1f8a69ebc28da200c\nparent e142be077f0c727ab11ba51ecaba9a98b7bfe474\nauthor Clark Zinzow <clarkzinzow@gmail.com> 1665074536 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1665074536 -0500\n\n[Datasets] Bundle blocks smaller than batch size in `map_batches` tasks. (#28648)\n\nWhen blocks are smaller than the batch size in map_batches(), the actual size of batches provided to the UDF can be much smaller (order of magnitude) than the specified batch size, resulting in very poor batch mapping throughput when the UDF's performance is sensitive to the batch size (such as in batch inference on GPUs).\r\n\r\nThis PR optimistically sends multiple blocks to a single mapper task up to (but not past) the provided batch size, mitigating the case in which block size << batch size without needing a shuffle step.", "verified_at": "2024-01-16T19:59:59Z"}}, "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/commits/b5687a1aaa3dc72dfde9758e730607a4ab22afe4", "html_url": "https://github.com/ray-project/ray/commit/b5687a1aaa3dc72dfde9758e730607a4ab22afe4", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ray-project/ray/commits/b5687a1aaa3dc72dfde9758e730607a4ab22afe4/comments", "author": {"login": "clarkzinzow", "id": 7699919, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjc2OTk5MTk=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7699919?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/clarkzinzow", "html_url": "https://github.com/clarkzinzow", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/clarkzinzow/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/clarkzinzow/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/clarkzinzow/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/clarkzinzow/st